## Technical Design Tiers

- **Small** (single module, no API/DB change): brief notes in the feature Issue.
- **Medium** (API change or multi-module): one-page design in the feature Issue; 1-2 peer reviews before coding.
- **Large (single repo)** (DB schema, new tech, architectural impact): `docs/design/NNNN-short-name.md` reviewed via PR.
- **Cross-repo**: `<engineering-repo>/designs/NNNN-short-name.md` reviewed by owners of all affected repos.

## Security and Release Boundaries

- Never commit secrets, API keys, `.env` files, or credentials; `gitleaks` runs on every PR.
- Never delete, move, or re-push published `v*` tags.
- Do not modify deployment credentials or production environment rules inside business repositories; follow the ops repository handbook for releases and rollbacks.
